## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to design multi-tenant memory management with QoS, ensuring fairness under NUMA pressure and bursty workloads.

## Key Concepts

- Per-tenant fault quotas and replenishment
- Page fault path and concurrency control
- NUMA-aware per-core queues to reduce contention
- CAS/atomic updates for credits and queues
- Aging to prevent starvation under bursts

## Code Example

```c
// Minimal sketch
struct tenant {
  atomic_int credits;
  struct queue dq;
};

void handle_fault(struct tenant *t) {
  int old = atomic_fetch_sub(&t->credits, 1);
  if (old > 0) {
    service_fault_io();
  } else {
    atomic_fetch_add(&t->credits, 1);
    enqueue(&t->dq, current_fault);
  }
}
```

